  "summary": "The distinctive educational illustration style of Carson-Dellosa Publishing, known for bold outlines, bright colors, and friendly characters.",
  "description": "Carson-Dellosa Art Style refers to the visual language of Carson-Dellosa Publishing, a major American educational materials company. The style is characterized by bold black outlines, flat bright colors, rounded friendly characters, and clear simple compositions designed for classroom and children's educational products. It encompasses bulletin board sets, classroom decorations, workbooks, and teaching aids. The aesthetic is instantly recognizable in American elementary education and has become a nostalgic visual reference for Millennial and Gen-X childhood.",
